  "body": "Found in the #626 lathe investigation; shared by Fanuc Lathe and PathPilot output.\n\n**Today:**\n- **No rapid approach:** `crates/motion/src/turning/face.rs:205-209` starts a PathBuilder at `(rho_clear, clearance)` but never emits a move there. The first posted move is a **feed** to `(rho_clear, s + r)` from wherever the turret parked (`G01 X28 Z1.8 F0.0508`). That is an unplanned, unchecked path.\n- **Dragging retract:** each pass ends with a rapid back out radially at the Z just cut (`face.rs:219-221`), so the nose drags across the fresh face.\n\n**Expected:** a rapid to the clearance point before the first plunge, and a small Z lift (e.g. +0.2 mm) before the radial rapid out.\n\n**Done means:** facing goldens show `G0` to clearance, then the feed in, and each retract lifts Z first.",
